From: KRdp displayless experiment <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] libx264: constrain the advertised H.264 level to 5.2

KPipeWire asks libx264 for Baseline profile but leaves the H.264 level
unconstrained. With FFmpeg 8/libx264 this produces an SPS declaring level
6.0 (level_idc=60), even for an ordinary 1024x768 KRdp virtual output.

FreeRDP's OpenH264 decoder supports levels through 5.2 and rejects that SPS;
it consequently discards every RDPGFX AVC420 surface update. Level 5.2
covers the intended headless virtual outputs (up to 4096x2160 at 60 fps) and
is accepted by OpenH264. Keep the setting local to libx264; hardware and
libopenh264 encoders retain their own capability selection.

--- a/src/libx264encoder.cpp
+++ b/src/libx264encoder.cpp
@@ -66,6 +66,10 @@ bool LibX264Encoder::initialize(const QSize &size)
     m_avCodecContext->pix_fmt = AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P;
     m_avCodecContext->time_base = AVRational{1, 1000};

+    // An unconstrained libx264 level defaults to 6.0 with recent FFmpeg.
+    // OpenH264 (used by FreeRDP/Remmina) supports AVC only through 5.2.
+    m_avCodecContext->level = 52;
+
     switch (m_profile) {
